"]}, "overview": "Utah's first district is a brand-new seat created by redistricting, drawn with a roughly 12-point Democratic lean. Former congressman Ben McAdams, a moderate Democrat, faces Riley Owen, a Republican with minimal fundraising, in a race that has drawn heavy debate coverage across Utah media. McAdams won an expensive primary and has a large cash and outside-spending advantage.\n\nThe September Lighthouse poll of likely voters shows McAdams ahead by more than 40 points, and prediction markets give him a 96 to 98 percent chance of winning. Fundamentals, money, and markets all align on a comfortable Democratic hold, with the main uncertainty being how the new district behaves in its first election.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9908, "margin": 20.9}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.99, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9893, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9909, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9895, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9899, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9906, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9886, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9895, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9907, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.99, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9979, "margin": 28.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9958, "margin": 26.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.997, "margin": 27.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9991, "margin": 28.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9988, "margin": 27.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9979, "margin": 27.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9971, "margin": 27.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.9972, "margin": 26.0}]}